ADJUDICATION -- what the mechanical pass finds, and what it CANNOT find.

A1. Irrational.clear_of_ratio declared TWICE, lines 17 and 125, statement AND proof
    byte-identical, in namespaces IrrationalDemo and IrrationalCascade. The kernel
    accepts it because the namespaces differ. Genuine duplication.

A2/A3. SmallOrders.three_first_isolation = VersionB.order_three, and the four_ pair.
    VersionB's own header says it is a SECOND development of the proved cases --
    'Version B for the proved cases' -- so these are deliberate alternatives, not
    accidents. Worth knowing they are the same proposition; not a defect.

B. The five same-shape families are mostly small-order statements at different n
   (two_diffs / three_diffs / four_diffs). Same shape, different content.

THE LIMIT, and it is the important one. This pass compares TEXT. It cannot see a
mirror written in different types. The clearest example is one created on 2026-09-17:

   clear_of_residue_band   naturals, band as  m*(n*k+1) mod (n*e) in [e, (n-1)*e]
   clear_at_opening_of_band  reals, band as   exists M, n*M+1 <= (d/e)*(n*k+1) <= n*M+n-1

   'x mod m in [a,b]' and 'exists M, m*M+a <= x <= m*M+b' are the SAME condition, so
   the second is a generalisation of the first. It was proved from scratch that day
   without checking whether the tree already had it. The detector scores them as
   unrelated because the types and the spelling differ.

So the count below is a LOWER BOUND on the mirroring, and the cases it misses are
exactly the ones worth finding -- same mathematics, different dress.
